\f0\fs24 \cf0 # ADR-003: Queue-Based Reservation Processing\
\
## Status\
\
Accepted\
\
## Context\
\
The tutor will evaluate the Reservation API using JMeter with between 100 and 10,000 concurrent users.\
\
Traditional optimistic and pessimistic database locking mechanisms were considered.\
\
However, heavy lock contention may reduce performance under high load.\
\
## Decision\
\
Reservation requests will first enter a reservation queue.\
\
A Reservation Worker will process requests in a controlled manner.\
\
Architecture:\
\
Client\
   \uc0\u8595 \
Reservation API\
   \uc0\u8595 \
Concurrency Manager\
   \uc0\u8595 \
Reservation Queue\
   \uc0\u8595 \
Reservation Worker\
   \uc0\u8595 \
PostgreSQL\
\
## Consequences\
\
Advantages:\
\
- Better concurrency control\
- Reduced lock contention\
- Improved scalability\
- Predictable processing\
\
Disadvantages:\
\
- Slight increase in latency\
- Additional architectural component\
\
## Justification\
\
Queue-based processing provides a more scalable approach for handling reservation spikes while maintaining data consistency.}